  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column of the cash receipts statement (p5). Taxes 1,207,868 split into property tax, penalties, PPD sales tax and motor vehicle using the General Fund budget schedule (p8). Other Local Receipts and Intermediate Sources split using p8 lines. Non-Revenue Receipts 22,934 split using the fund budget schedules (pp9, 11, 12, 14): sale of property 1,000, insurance adjustments 1,824, other non-revenue receipts 20,110 (unexplained). Zero-amount lines (printed as dashes) are omitted from receipts, disbursements and detail; General Fund lines with only a budget amount are omitted from detail. Transfers: Activities 33,194 + Nutrition 11,436 = 44,630 matches General Fund transfer out (p9, p10); the General Fund budget schedule total disbursements 5,401,849 include the 44,630 transfer, recorded as other financing -44,630 in detail. Printed totals differ from line sums by 1-2 dollars (rounding), recorded in report_discrepancies. The General Fund Components statement (p6) and County Treasurer schedule (p16, pass-through of tax receipts) not added to detail to avoid double counting. No liabilities printed. Budget amounts printed as dashes recorded as null. The added trimmed p7 (combining balance sheet, other governmental funds: Activities 155,165 and School Nutrition 58,368 cash and assigned fund balances, total 213,533) ties to the governmental funds balance sheet and adds no detail lines. State Sources 3,426,595 (p5) split using the General Fund schedule (p9): Homestead Exemption 16,233, Property Tax Credit 713,013, Motor Vehicle Pro-Rate 3,808, remaining state aid 2,693,541 (fixed 2026-10-27). Balance sheet (user 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets, liabilities and fund balances (p4), Total Governmental Funds column. Read pages 1-17 of 17"
}